.TH HD-LAUNCHER 8 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-launcher \- write the menu of the application launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-launcher
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-launcher
writes the menu of the application launcher of the HyprDebian desktop,
.IR /var/cache/hd-launcher/launcher.json ,
the input of
.BR hd-menu (1),
from the
.I .desktop
files in
.I /usr/share/applications
and its subdirectories, and the items added in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json .
.PP
An application is in the menu when its
.I .desktop
file is of the
.B Type
Application, has a
.B Name
and an
.BR Exec ,
is not
.B NoDisplay
or
.BR Hidden ,
is not left out for Hyprland by
.B OnlyShowIn
or
.BR NotShowIn ,
has its
.B TryExec
installed, when it has one, and is not left out by the key
.B hd-launcher
(see CONFIGURATION).
.PP
The menu is 40% of the width and the height of the output; the options that
do not fit scroll.
Every application and every item added is an option, with its
.B Name
or
.B name
as the label.
The value is the command line that starts it as a systemd user unit of its
own, quoted for the shell, which the launcher runs with
.BR "sh \-c" :
.B uwsm app \-\-
with the desktop file ID of an application, such as
.IR firefox.desktop ,
or the command of an item added.
The ID of a file in a subdirectory is its path below
.I /usr/share/applications
with \- for /.
The options are sorted on the label, in ascending order, without regard to
case.
.PP
The icon of an application is looked up by its
.B Icon
in the icon themes hicolor and Adwaita and in
.IR /usr/share/pixmaps ,
or taken from its path when it is one.
A PNG is used as it is.
An SVG is rendered to a PNG of the
.B icon_size
of the
.B hd-theme
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
64 without one, in
.IR /var/cache/hd-launcher/icons ;
only when the PNG there was not rendered from that SVG at that size.
The icons of applications that are gone or left out are removed.
.PP
The apt hook
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/90hd-launcher
runs
.B hd-launcher
each time apt has run dpkg: after an installation, an upgrade or a removal.
A failure is reported but does not fail apt.
The installation of
.BR hd-desktop (7)
runs it too.
After another theme is selected, with another
.BR icon_size ,
run it again.
.PP
Run it as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n ,\  \-\-dry\-run
Print the menu that would be written, write nothing; it may be run by any
user.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The key
.B hd-launcher
of
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
leaves applications out of the menu and adds items of its own:
.PP
.RS
.nf
"hd-launcher": {
    "exclude": ["org.gnome.Meld.desktop", "debian-xterm"],
    "add": [
        {
            "name": "Btop",
            "command": ["kitty", "\-e", "btop"],
            "icon": "utilities-system-monitor"
        }
    ]
}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B exclude
Optional: the desktop file IDs to leave out; the
.I .desktop
at the end may be left out.
.TP
.B add
Optional: the items to add, each an object with:
.RS
.TP
.B name
The label.
.TP
.B command
The words of the command, a list of strings, run without a shell.
For pipes, variables or
.IR ~ ,
use
.BR "[\(dqsh\(dq, \(dq\-c\(dq, \(dq...\(dq]" .
.TP
.B icon
Optional: the path of a PNG or SVG, or the name of an icon, looked up as the
.B Icon
of an application.
An icon that is not found is reported and left out.
.RE
.PP
Other members, or a key that is not such an object, are an error: the menu
is not written.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/cache/hd-launcher/launcher.json
The menu, for
.BR hd-menu (1).
.TP
.I /var/cache/hd-launcher/icons
The PNGs rendered from SVG icons.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/90hd-launcher
The apt hook.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The applications to leave out and the items to add, in the key
.BR hd-launcher ,
and the
.BR icon_size ,
in the key
.BR hd-theme .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the menu was written, 1 on an error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-desktop (7),
.BR hd-menu (1),
.BR hd-theme (7),
.BR hd-config (7)
